+# Catalog
+
+For whoever changes pantry search or investigates stale stock on the item page. Catalog search returns matching
+pantry items in name order; repeated searches can use Redis because the page is slow on Saturday mornings.
+
+## Search results
+
+[`larder/catalog.py`](../../larder/catalog.py) owns the search query and cache implementation. Results include item
+id, name and stock. The cache stores the whole result, including empty searches, under a versioned hash of the exact
+query. It uses JSON rather than executable serialization. Hits skip the database query; misses and invalid entries
+are replaced from Postgres. A cache read failure skips the cache write for that request.
+
+## Known limits
+
+- Results, including stock and empty results, can be stale for 15 seconds after being cached. Expiry refreshes them
+  on the next request; this browsing cache must not be used to validate stock when confirming an order.
+- Simultaneous misses can each query Postgres. There is no lock or protection against a burst of distinct searches;
+  measure the Saturday workload to establish whether additional query tuning is needed.
+- The key assumes one shared pantry database. Separate deployments or databases need separate Redis databases to
+  prevent sharing catalog results.
+
+## Shaped by
+
+- [Cache catalog results in Redis](../adr/0003-cache-catalog-results-in-redis.md)
+- [Enable or disable the catalog cache](../runbooks/catalog-cache.md)
